## Examples

```shell
pixi audit
pixi audit --environment prod --platform linux-64
pixi audit --fail-on high # (1)!
pixi audit --format sarif > pixi-audit.sarif # (2)!
pixi audit --fix # (3)!
```

1. Only vulnerability matches rated high or critical fail the audit. Matches with unknown severity always fail.
2. Upload the report to GitHub code scanning. Ignored matches are included as suppressions.
3. Solve once with temporary constraints and replace the lock file only when every vulnerability match then passes the policy. The manifest is never edited.

See [Auditing for vulnerabilities](../../security.md#auditing-for-vulnerabilities) for the policy, coverage, and remediation details.

